All discovered flaws and UI layer issues have been thoroughly investigated, diagnosed, and resolved.
1. Root Cause & Fix for the "Two Layers" at the Bottom of Class Group Selection
What occurred in screenshot & code: In ClassGroupSelectionScreen (OnboardingScreens.kt), Modifier.navigationBarsPadding() had been placed directly on the outer Surface of the bottomBar. This constrained the white Surface to stop strictly above the navigation bar area, leaving the system navigation bar strip exposed with the Scaffold's greyish background showing behind it, plus an 8.dp elevation shadow cast downward across that boundary. It created a visually detached, floating card effect with a second layer visible underneath near the gesture bar.
The Solution:
The Surface now docks solidly all the way to the bottom physical edge of the display (modifier = Modifier.fillMaxWidth()) with a clean top divider line (MaterialTheme.colorScheme.outlineVariant.copy(alpha = 0.5f)).
navigationBarsPadding() was moved inside the Surface onto the inner content Box (.navigationBarsPadding().padding(horizontal = 20.dp, vertical = 16.dp)).
The bottom dock is now a continuous, solid, unified surface extending behind the Android navigation gesture pill with zero cut-off or underlayer gap.
